<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  MAIDR Chart on Slide: the content add-in MAIDR publishes for PowerPoint. It
  sits on a slide as a shape, beside one of PowerPoint's own charts or over
  it, and shows MAIDR's figure for that chart, in Normal view and in the
  slide show. See docs/office-addin.md for installing it, and
  addin/README.md for how it is built and served.

  A separate add-in from the task pane's (manifest.xml), with an Id of its
  own: one manifest describes a task pane add-in or a content add-in, never
  both. It has no ribbon button. It is inserted on a slide from Home >
  Add-ins (Insert > My Add-ins in older versions), and RequestedWidth and
  RequestedHeight are the size it starts at.

  Every URL is on https://maidr.ai/: the page and the icons are under
  /addin/, where the documentation site serves this folder
  (scripts/build-site.js), and the support page is the users' guide. The page
  loads MAIDR from the same site's dist/ and calls
  maidrOffice.bindSlideChart, which reads the chart from the presentation
  file and keeps which chart it reads as one of the add-in's settings, in the
  presentation.

  ReadWriteDocument, although the add-in changes nothing on the slides:
  reading the file (Document.getFileAsync) takes ReadAllDocument, and
  following PowerPoint into the slide show (Document.addHandlerAsync) takes
  ReadWriteDocument, as every event does.

  AllowSnapshot, which is Office's default, saves a picture of the add-in
  with the presentation, so a PowerPoint that cannot run it shows what it
  last showed rather than an empty box. The picture is whatever the box
  showed last: usually the chart's name and the add-in's controls, which name
  only what the file holds anyway, but it can hold one of MAIDR's dialogs
  left open there, such as the AI chat with the reader's questions, as
  Microsoft warns (AllowSnapshot in the manifest reference). The users'
  guide's privacy section says so.

  Change the Version whenever this file changes, as Office and the Microsoft
  Marketplace require. Keep the Id: it is the add-in's identity everywhere it
  has been installed, and in every presentation it has been inserted in.
-->
<OfficeApp
  xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/appforoffice/1.1"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:type="ContentApp">
  <Id>fa16e8d3-7524-43fa-a436-3156caba8b6f</Id>
  <Version>1.0.0.0</Version>
  <ProviderName>xability</ProviderName>
  <DefaultLocale>en-US</DefaultLocale>
  <DisplayName DefaultValue="MAIDR Chart on Slide" />
  <Description DefaultValue="Hear, read in braille and explore with the keyboard a chart on a slide, in Normal view and in the slide show: MAIDR reads PowerPoint's own chart, for blind and low-vision presenters and readers." />
  <IconUrl DefaultValue="https://maidr.ai/addin/assets/icon-32.png" />
  <HighResolutionIconUrl DefaultValue="https://maidr.ai/addin/assets/icon-64.png" />
  <SupportUrl DefaultValue="https://maidr.ai/office-addin.html" />
  <Hosts>
    <Host Name="Presentation" />
  </Hosts>
  <DefaultSettings>
    <SourceLocation DefaultValue="https://maidr.ai/addin/slide.html" />
    <RequestedWidth>480</RequestedWidth>
    <RequestedHeight>270</RequestedHeight>
  </DefaultSettings>
  <Permissions>ReadWriteDocument</Permissions>
  <AllowSnapshot>true</AllowSnapshot>
</OfficeApp>
